    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Bladewing Blood Bat Gu sits in the Blood Sea Ancestor’s blood path legacy: after naming bladewing blood bat, blood frenzy Gu, and blood guillotine as his fusion recipes, the Ancestor’s dying line is that the blood path is not alone and that the legacy will continue for all eternity. Bladewing blood bat Gu also counts among the easy leftovers found in his inheritance grounds, alongside those other two Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          183
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "path_blood"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "They are blood colored bats with two long pointed ears and two pairs of wings. The main pair is rather big. The secondary pair is smaller and sits below the main wings. They have no claws. The edges of both pairs of wings are as sharp as steel blades.",
        "chapters": [
          183
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Male and female bats look the same.",
        "chapters": [
          188
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The bats are rank three at first sight of that colony.",
        "chapters": [
          183
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Male and female bats look the same; only familiarity lets Fang Yuan tell them apart.",
        "chapters": [
          188
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "The colony of bladewing blood bats is special: a Gu Master who controls a male bat can indirectly command the other female bats.",
        "chapters": [
          183
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In a blood bat group there is only one male; without that male the whole group falls into chaos.",
        "chapters": [
          188
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Righteous Gu pressure leaves the bats frantic and struggling to stay aloft, which keeps them from hunting Fang Yuan for a time.",
        "chapters": [
          184
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-battles",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_righteous_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "First gen Gu Yue brings almost a thousand bladewing blood bats out of the blood lake and cave ceiling against Tie Xue Leng’s giant puppet, together with rank five Blood Guillotine. The bats are rank three close-combat Gu whose numbers can pressure even a rank five opponent, but rank six Gu aura dominates them completely. Under a Gu Master’s command the bat army holds formation; without that control the difference is stark. Heaven Earth Magnificent Sound Gu, used at full power through the puppet, kills nearby bladewing blood bat Gu and throws farther groups into disorder.",
        "chapters": [
          186
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-battles",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_tie_xue_leng",
          "gu_blood_guillotine_gu",
          "gu_heaven_earth_magnificent_sound_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In a narrow tunnel Fang Yuan faces close to a hundred bats without First gen Gu Yue present. Internal friction among uncontrolled bats leaves him fighting only thirty to forty at once, and he kills the sole male of that group with Chainsaw Golden Centipede to scatter the rest.",
        "chapters": [
          187
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-battles",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_chainsaw_golden_centipede"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "First gen Gu Yue later sends bat groups to seize Fang Yuan for the Heavenly Essence Treasure Lotus.",
        "chapters": [
          188
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-battles",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_heavenly_essence_treasure_lotus"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan kills the male of one group, scatters the rest, and uses polluted Thunderwings Gu as bait while he flees. The bats fly too fast, with wings sharp like blades, for him to capture any without an iron hand grappling Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          188
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-battles",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_thunderwings_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Lord Sky Crane later rages that both the blood guillotine and the bladewing blood bat Gu were supposed to be his, after First gen Gu Yue sent countless bats with the guillotines against the crane flock. Beside Blood Guillotine, the bats are much smaller than Iron Beak Flying Cranes and gain movement advantage from that size. First gen Gu Yue orders blood guillotine and bladewing blood bat Gu to cut Raise Eyebrows and Exhale Gu’s white eyebrows, then turns them on Lord Sky Crane when cutting fails.",
        "chapters": [
          192
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-battles",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_lord_sky_crane",
          "gu_raise_eyebrows_and_exhale_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When Lord Sky Crane attacks the village, First gen Gu Yue pulls the bats and guillotines back to defend it.",
        "chapters": [
          193
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-battles",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "He still later sends large numbers of them against a glacier to slow it.",
        "chapters": [
          195
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qing-mao-mountain-battles",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
  "feeding": {
    "known": true,
    "food_raw": null,
    "foods": [],
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "The Gu is very easy to feed. Its food is blood, but it still needs the Gu Master to supply primeval essence. Like Blood Frenzy Gu and blood guillotine, it is easy to raise and multiply, and leftover copies can turn up in Blood Sea Ancestor inheritance grounds from valleys and villages to deserts and mountain paths.",
        "chapters": [
          183
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "feeding",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_blood_frenzy_gu",
          "char_blood_sea_ancestor"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
