  "distribution": {
    "locations": [
      "reg_southern_border"
    ],
    "factions": [],
    "origin": "unknown",
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Bladewing blood bat was the Blood Sea Ancestor’s first fusion accomplishment, ahead of blood frenzy Gu and blood guillotine. He was a rank seven demonic path Gu Master researching Gu that could still absorb natural primeval essence after refinement; this recipe was the earliest of the three he finished before righteous path traps defeated him. After fatal wounds he seeded hundreds of thousands of inheritance grounds from the Middle Continent to the Southern Border and elsewhere.",
        "chapters": [
          183
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "origin-under-blood-sea-ancestor",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "reg_southern_border"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In Fang Yuan’s previous life, after over four hundred years, he obtained a Blood Sea Ancestor inheritance, used colonies of these bats with rank five cultivation to become a regional overlord, and made the bladewing blood bat the symbol of Bloodwing Devil Sect, which could support close to ten thousand of them. On Qing Mao Mountain he wonders whether Flower Wine Monk’s near-death wounds in the Photo-audio Gu image came from these bats rather than Moonshadow Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          183
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "origin-under-blood-sea-ancestor",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_flower_wine_monk",
          "gu_photo_audio_gu",
          "gu_moonshadow_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "That guess is never confirmed. An intense battle with First gen Gu Yue and an escape along the Thousand Li Earthwolf Spider path instead account for the Monk’s blood-bathed state.",
        "chapters": [
          188
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "origin-under-blood-sea-ancestor",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_first_gen_gu_yue",
          "gu_thousand_li_earthwolf_spider"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
