  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan meets hundreds of blood-colored bats rising from a blood lake under Qing Mao Mountain and names them rank three bladewing blood bat Gu. Each bat has two long pointed ears and two pairs of wings, a larger main pair and a smaller secondary pair below, with no claws and wing edges as sharp as steel blades.",
        "chapters": [
          183
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "loc_qing_mao_mountain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "While training dog groups for San Cha Mountain, he recalls commanding numerous beast groups across five hundred years, especially blade-wing blood bats from the Blood Sea inheritance.",
        "chapters": [
          346
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "prior-life-command-skill",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_san_cha_mountain",
          "inh_blood_sea_inheritance"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Jiang Wan Shan tells Dong Fang Yu Liang he was not an enslavement path Gu Master from the start. He found a Blood Sea Ancestor small inheritance on an expedition, obtained a bladewing blood bats group there, and has been gathering relevant enslavement path Gu worms slowly ever since.",
        "chapters": [
          506
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "jiang-wan-shan-in-northern-plains",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_jiang_wan_shan",
          "char_dong_fang_yu_liang",
          "sys_gu_worms"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In the later battle his four-winged blood-colored bats join with knife-sharp wings, and Fang Yuan names the force Jiang Wan Shan’s bladewing blood bats group. Fang Yuan then calls that group’s offensive power very sharp and notes that his wolf group cannot answer aerial attacks.",
        "chapters": [
          511
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "jiang-wan-shan-in-northern-plains",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After that Northern Plains battle the novel does not show another on-stage colony of Bladewing Blood Bat Gu under a new named holder.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "jiang-wan-shan-in-northern-plains",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "reg_northern_plains"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
